  "description": "Apple Pay and Google Pay (CONTRACT §17, revision 7). Inputs are what the SDK sees; expect is what it must produce. JSON objects under expect are compared as JSON values (key order and white space do not matter). order objects are the GET order payload (§16.3); wrap them in the usual {\"code\":\"00000\",\"payload\":…} envelope when a test needs a response. amount is a JSON number, as the API sends it. X-Client-App-Id is the platform's own example id. Revision 10: availability no longer checks paymentMethods; see platformGuard and googlePayGateway.",
